---
args: { desk: SourcingDesk, book: NegotiationBook | null }
returns: NegotiationRound
---
Bind prior to the supplied book or a complete empty NegotiationBook at revision zero with empty candidates, replies, envelopes, commitments and consumed-evidence lists, an empty mandate version and null approvedFx. Preserve every old dispatch receipt and source version. Bind mandate = readBuyerMandate(desk, prior) and initialize offers: QuoteOption[] = [], replies: TermReply[] = [], candidates: PackageCandidate[] = [], acceptances: PackageAcceptance[] = [], outbound: SupplierEnvelope[] = [], and questions to mandate.unresolved.

If mandate.changed, bind outbound = suspendUnapprovedOffers(prior, mandate, desk.quotations). Suspend unsent drafts; sent or unknown envelopes retain their actual status and need scoped withdrawal/readback. Do not parse new offers or create counteroffers under a changed mandate. Set action = "suspend-outstanding" and keep prior candidate, reply, commitment and approved-FX histories.

Otherwise bind offers = readQuotationBook(desk, mandate) and replies = reconcileSupplierReplies(desk.quotations, prior.candidates, mandate). Apply each qualified reply only to its named term; reopen every package depending on a changed condition. Bind candidates = searchFeasiblePackages(desk, offers, replies, mandate). Keep unfilled demand, incompatible bundles and unresolved prices explicit. If mandate.unresolved or any candidate has unresolved authority, conversion or commitment prerequisites, set action = "await-authority", keep outbound empty, and add the exact blockers to questions. No incomplete package may generate an offer.

When authority, offer validity and exact conversion bases are adequate, for each candidate bind one acceptance = recheckCommitmentBoundary(candidate, offers, replies, mandate, prior). A complete acceptance requires current binding offers, configured signature evidence and the exact approved conversion basis. If any candidate has a complete acceptance, set action = "ready-to-sign" and preserve only its exact outstanding terms and signature evidence in the buyer brief; do not mark a commitment until the signed agreement receipt is present. Otherwise bind outbound = proposeSealedCounteroffers(candidates, mandate, prior), set action = "bargain", and keep a separate sealed envelope for each supplier without disclosing rival terms.

Bind nextBook: NegotiationBook = { revision: advance only when the mandate version, candidate set, term replies, envelopes, commitment receipts or consumed evidence changed; otherwise preserve prior.revision, mandateVersion: mandate.version, candidates: append or revise only by exact package and offer identity while preserving superseded editions, replies: append each source-identified supplier term response once, envelopes: update only the exact suspended or revised envelope identities while retaining all dispatch receipts, committedPackageIds: prior IDs plus only package IDs with actual matching signed agreement receipts, approvedFx: prior.approvedFx unchanged, consumedEvidenceIds: prior identities plus newly consumed source identities }. Bind buyerBrief to the buyer-authorized mandate constraints, feasible package tradeoffs, and actual acceptance or blocker results; never include one supplier's confidential terms in another supplier's envelope. Bind questions to mandate questions, package blockers, and each acceptance's outstanding terms or the exact external status readback required.

Return { book: nextBook, mandate, action, buyerBrief, questions, outbound } as NegotiationRound. A suspension or authority hold still returns the full round and preserves old commitments; external dispatch and signature receipts enter only as evidence in a later round.
